# Intent: the pure logic of the unit's own sounds (owner approved the sound plan on 2026-11-13, docs/dev/stackchan-lights-audit-and-plan-2026-11-13.md sections 14 and 17). One header of plain C99 with no hardware in it: the fixed list of twelve sound names (the seven new earcons needs_you, plug_in, charged, unplug, offline, goodbye, shutter and the five shipped tones success, popup, vibration, exclamation, low_battery); the one gate that says whether a sound may play (sounds off, the hard mute, quiet hours that may wrap midnight, the host's "it is night" verdict that is trusted only while Home is up, robot.sounds.night, and which cues are allowed in the night: shutter, goodbye, low_battery, exclamation, the wake and tap tones, and needs_you only at first setup); the charger events from the AXP2101 facts (plug in, unplug, full, each after three polls agree, none on the first poll, "full" only after charging was seen); the link state the offline phrases follow (no Wi-Fi, connecting, no host, refused), with the outage clock that decides the offline earcon and the "I'm back" clip (over a minute); and the phrase picker for sixteen clips in five groups: a round robin so no clip repeats in a row, at most one per 10 s and three in any minute, the tone only at night or past the limit, nothing when muted. Times are passed in, so it is wrap safe and testable.
